        faqA4: 'ETERNAL VOID designs continuously and independently. Submitting does not stop us from developing our own work, including work that resembles yours. What the intake terms do is keep your submission out of production unless we sign an agreement with you for it.',
        faqQ5: 'How long do you keep my files?',
        faqA5: 'Uploaded files are kept while the submission is under review and for a limited retention period after it is closed, then deleted. The exact period is stated in the Submission Privacy Notice. You can ask us to withdraw and delete earlier at any time.',
        faqQ6: 'Do I have to be a professional designer?',
        faqA6: 'No. The programme exists for emerging designers and artists. You need to be old enough to enter a contract where you live, and the work needs to be yours.',
        faqQ7: 'Do I need a tech pack to submit?',
        faqA7: 'No. A sketch is enough to apply. A full, production-ready tech pack is needed only from a selected artist, together with a signed collaboration agreement, to qualify for the proposed 12% royalty on net profit. You are welcome to include one now; it does not guarantee selection, production or payment.',
        faqQ8: 'How is the royalty calculated?',
        faqA8: 'The proposed royalty is 12% of the net profit from sales of your specific design: sales after discounts and refunds, excluding VAT and separately charged shipping, less documented manufacturing, printing, packaging and payment-processing costs for the units sold. For example, €1,000 in eligible sales less €400 in eligible costs gives €600 profit and a €72 royalty. Sampling, marketing and overhead are never deducted.',
        faqQ9: 'What if someone else submitted my work?',
        faqA9: 'If you believe work submitted here is yours and was sent by someone else, write to <a href="mailto:legal@eternalvoid.co">legal@eternalvoid.co</a>. Tell us what the work is and what your claim is. We suspend review of the submission while we look into it.',
